  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-PAK802</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO supports workers&apos; organizations in implementing the priority areas of the Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP) through capacity building in various areas such as policy development, advocacy, labour law reforms, social dialogue, compliance, and outreach. Technical advice is provided to enhance workers&#x2019; organizations&#x2019; ability to serve domestic workers, focusing on campaigns to raise awareness about rights and responsibilities, while increasing their organization and representation. Digital platforms are being used to expand awareness and reach.

Key technical areas identified by workers&#x2019; organizations include Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work, negotiation skills, occupational safety and health (OSH), paralegal work, and gender inclusion. Capacity building efforts emphasize improving workers&apos; access to supply chains, which is crucial in areas where labour legislation is weak or absent. Social mobilization by workers&#x2019; organizations plays a critical role in protecting workers and vulnerable groups from exploitation.

Ongoing capacity building includes training cohorts of trainers on subjects like social protection, safe migration, and FPRW. This biennium will focus on organizing workers in the informal economy, expanding access through digital tools, and using innovative strategies to increase awareness. Collaboration with employers&apos; organizations will contribute to platforms such as the MNED focal point, WEBCOP, and dialogues with the UN for the implementation of the UN Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework (UNSDCF).</narrative>
  </description>
